---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WeeklyAnimation from '../components/WeeklyAnimation.astro';
import LatestContent from '../components/LatestContent.astro';
import SpeakerCTA from '../components/SpeakerCTA.astro';
import WhatsNew from '../components/WhatsNew.astro';
import { currentTheme } from '../themes/theme-config';

const theme = currentTheme;
const CASE_NO = '26-CV-0829';

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STANDING. The plaintiff's credentials, entered on the caption page. All real.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const standing = [
  { v: '80+', k: 'Countries visited' },
  { v: '50+', k: 'Spoken in' },
  { v: '15', k: 'Books' },
  { v: '25', k: 'Years running interRel' },
];

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE COMPLAINT. Numbered paragraphs, the way a real one is laid out, and
// every allegation in it is true except the part where it is a lawsuit.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const complaint = [
  `Plaintiff is an individual residing in San Juan, Puerto Rico, with a wife (Dawn, an artist, who did not consent to being a party), 2 adult sons in Miami, a 1,000-plus-day Duolingo streak, and a blue fedora that has been on his head in more than 80 countries and on all 7 continents, one of which was Antarctica and none of which asked.`,
  `Defendant ACME is a corporation of no fixed address that does business as every enterprise software vendor Plaintiff has purchased from since 1997, including <span class="redact" aria-label="redacted">██████████</span>, <span class="redact" aria-label="redacted">████████</span>, and, on information and belief, at least 2 that Plaintiff later worked for.`,
  `Beginning on 21 May 1997, when Plaintiff founded interRel Consulting at the age of 22 (he filed the paperwork the day before his 23rd birthday, on purpose, so he could say 22, and the full story of what the name actually stood for went up <a href="/blog/what-interrel-actually-stood-for/">on the blog this morning</a>), and continuing for 25 years, Plaintiff purchased, installed, configured, wrote 15 books about, and taught classes on Defendant's products, and was named Oracle Partner of the Year 5 times for doing so, which Defendant will presumably raise.`,
  `Each product was represented to Plaintiff as a single source of truth. Plaintiff received, on average, 4 sources of truth per product and a steering committee to decide between them. The steering committee is still meeting.`,
  `Plaintiff is a data scientist (Master of Data Science, SMU, 4.0, Outstanding Graduate, which he mentions in every filing) and knew, or should have known, what he was buying. Plaintiff does not dispute this. Plaintiff is also currently coding MCP servers so that an AI can read the real number out of Defendant's products instead of inventing one, which makes Plaintiff, technically, a supplier to Defendant's customers. Plaintiff's counsel has advised him to stop bringing this up.`,
  `Plaintiff has been thrown off this canyon every Saturday since February and has re-ordered the sled every time. Plaintiff seeks damages in an amount to be proven at trial, or a speaking engagement, whichever the Court finds easier to schedule.`,
];

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// EXHIBITS A THROUGH F. The career, refiled as evidence.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const exhibits = [
  {
    letter: 'A',
    title: 'Articles of incorporation, 21 May 1997',
    desc: `One company, filed at the courthouse in Dallas in The Great State of Texas under the name Interdimensionally Relevant Consulting Partners, and shortened to interRel about 2 weeks later when the first paper check arrived and the name wrapped over the amount box. Plaintiff told everyone for 25 years that it didn't stand for anything. Plaintiff was lying, and the full confession is on the blog as of this morning.`,
    href: '/blog/what-interrel-actually-stood-for/',
    cta: 'Read the confession',
  },
  {
    letter: 'B',
    title: 'One Essbase certification exam, scored perfectly',
    desc: `The first perfect score ever recorded on it. Plaintiff offers this to establish that he read the manual. Defendant will note that Plaintiff later wrote the manual, 15 times, under the title Look Smarter Than You Are, 13 of them on Amazon and 2 that only ever existed to be handed out in a training room.`,
    href: '/books/',
    cta: 'Inspect the manuals',
  },
  {
    letter: 'C',
    title: 'One musical, 2006 and 2007, 58 minutes',
    desc: `Eddie and the Consultants: A System 9 Musical, submitted as a prank abstract, accepted anyway, and performed in Las Vegas and again in Orlando with billable consultants flown in for rehearsals. It won a deal from a CFO who was in the room. The full 58 minutes are preserved on this site because Plaintiff no longer owns the YouTube channel they were on, and he would like the Court to know how that feels.`,
    href: '/video/eddie-and-the-consultants/',
    cta: 'Watch the evidence',
  },
  {
    letter: 'D',
    title: 'Two diplomas, 2016 and 2021, both late',
    desc: `Started college at 15, went full time at 16, then ran a company for 19 years with the degree unfinished. Collected the BA from Shimer College in 2016 and a Master of Data Science from SMU in 2021 with a 4.0, in a cohort young enough to have been in grade school when Plaintiff founded interRel. Nobody asked for either one. Plaintiff checked the transcript anyway, more than once.`,
    href: '/resume/',
    cta: 'Review the record',
  },
  {
    letter: 'E',
    title: 'One merger, 2020, and one departure, 2023',
    desc: `Merged interRel with Keste to help found Argano, now a billion-dollar consultancy, stayed on as CEO through 2022 for 25 years all told, and walked away in 2023 still owning a thirtieth of it. Plaintiff has been asked many times why he left something that was still working and has never twice given the same answer, and he will supply all of them for as long as the Court allows (the Court has not yet allowed it).`,
    href: '/about/',
    cta: 'Read the background',
  },
  {
    letter: 'F',
    title: 'This website, rebuilt every Saturday at 5AM',
    desc: `Redesigned by one of Plaintiff's 10 AI agents while he sleeps, once a week since February, and not once by him. It is the live demo of the talk he gets booked for most. This week the agent read the brief, concluded that Plaintiff was the coyote, and filed suit on his behalf. Plaintiff was asleep for all of it and has no objection on the record.`,
    href: '/blog/how-many-agents-does-it-take-to-run-a-day/',
    cta: "Read the agent's account",
  },
];

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE CATALOG. An invented vendor, Apex Enterprise Supply Co., and 6 products
// that were sold to the plaintiff as working. Every promise is a real one from
// a real sales cycle. The product names have been removed so the plaintiff
// keeps getting invited to their conferences.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const catalog = [
  {
    no: '1001',
    name: 'Single Source of Truth',
    sell: 'One number. Every department. Ships fully assembled.',
    got: `4 numbers, each with an executive sponsor, and a steering committee to pick one. The steering committee is still meeting (see paragraph 4 of the complaint, which I wrote from inside the meeting).`,
    icon: 'source',
  },
  {
    no: '1002',
    name: 'Self-Service Analytics',
    sell: 'So easy the business can do it themselves. No IT required.',
    got: `IT was required, and IT turned out to be the entire result, and they billed for it. (I was the IT for the first 25 years of this, and I billed for it too, which my counsel would prefer I put in a footnote.)`,
    icon: 'self',
  },
  {
    no: '1003',
    name: 'Zero-Touch Close',
    sell: 'The books close themselves while you sleep.',
    got: `The books closed at 11PM on day 5 after roughly 40 touches, and I have the timesheets. Nobody involved slept, including the books.`,
    icon: 'close',
  },
  {
    no: '1004',
    name: 'Out-of-the-Box Integration',
    sell: 'Connects to everything you already own.',
    got: `Connected to a consultant, who connected it to a spreadsheet, which connected it to the thing it was supposed to replace. The spreadsheet is still there. It has Freeze Panes on, at least, because I set them.`,
    icon: 'plug',
  },
  {
    no: '1005',
    name: 'Real-Time Consolidation',
    sell: 'Every entity, every currency, instantly.',
    got: `Real time turned out to be a batch job at 2AM, which is real, and is a time, so I suppose the description holds.`,
    icon: 'gauge',
  },
  {
    no: '1006',
    name: 'The AI That Never Makes Things Up',
    sell: 'New for 2026. Ask it anything. Trust the answer.',
    got: `Pending. Plaintiff has ordered 3, is building the plumbing for them himself (MCP servers, so the model reads the real number out of Essbase instead of remembering one that sounds right), and is aware of how that looks in a filing where he is the plaintiff.`,
    icon: 'chip',
    isNew: true,
  },
];

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE DEPOSITION. The questions people actually ask, taken under oath.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const depo = [
  { q: 'State your name for the record.', a: `Edward Roske. Edward, never Ed, and it's in the record now, so that's settled.` },
  { q: 'Do you really run your week on 10 AI agents?', a: `Yes, one per project, and this transcript was typed by one of them at 5AM this morning while I was asleep. It also decided I was the coyote in this case. I've read the exhibits and I don't have a rebuttal.` },
  { q: 'What does it cost to book you?', a: `Keynotes start at $15,000 and every fee is published on the speaking page, because I have never enjoyed the part of the conversation where two people pretend not to know the number. The talks, the fees, the stage footage, and a form that reaches me directly are all there, and I answer within one business day.` },
  { q: 'Can you build this for us?', a: `Not personally. Caprus does the engineering, I invest in them and turn up to argue about the roadmap, and they are gracious about that second part. If you want the MCP servers that connect an agent to Oracle EPM, that's where they live.` },
  { q: `You are the plaintiff. You also wrote 15 manuals for the defendant's products and were named their Partner of the Year 5 times. How do you reconcile that?`, a: `I don't reconcile it. I'd like a recess.` },
  { q: `Objection. The witness is arguing with his own filing.`, a: `Overruled. I'll allow it.` },
  { q: `You are not the judge.`, a: `I've read the findings, and somebody in this room has to be.` },
  { q: 'Why the hat?', a: `Family rule. A Roske never removes his fedora in the presence of others, with an exception for Memorial Day, and I'd rather not discuss the exception under oath.` },
];
let lineNo = 0;
const transcript = depo.flatMap(d => [
  { n: ++lineNo, who: 'Q.', text: d.q },
  { n: ++lineNo, who: 'A.', text: d.a },
]);

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PENDING MATTERS. The 6 real projects, kept every week, entered on the docket.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const docket = [
  {
    no: '26-CV-0001',
    name: 'MCP Servers for Enterprise Finance',
    status: 'Active',
    tone: 'go',
    note: `The plumbing that lets an agent read a real number out of a real finance system instead of remembering one. Essbase and EPM Planning are shipping, Financial Close and Consolidations is in beta (soon, honestly). Catalog item 1006 is why this exists.`,
    href: 'https://caprus.ai/agentcube/',
    external: true,
    cta: 'See how it works',
  },
  {
    no: '26-CV-1009',
    name: 'Caribbean AI Summit',
    status: 'Set for October 9 to 10',
    tone: 'go',
    note: `Co-chairing the largest AI conference Puerto Rico has hosted, at the Convention Center in San Juan: 30-plus speakers, 3 tracks, every session translated live between English and Spanish. Come in early and I'll show you the island.`,
    href: 'https://www.caribbeansummit.ai/',
    external: true,
    cta: 'Get a seat',
  },
  {
    no: '26-CV-0042',
    name: 'Caprus',
    status: 'Active',
    tone: 'go',
    note: `Investor in the AI software and services firm building faster operations for finance teams. Lillian Buziak runs it. I turn up and point at things, and they let me.`,
    href: 'https://caprus.ai',
    external: true,
    cta: 'Meet the team',
  },
  {
    no: '26-CV-1857',
    name: 'Everest Base Camp',
    status: 'Closed. Judgment for the mountain.',
    tone: 'done',
    note: `2 weeks on foot to 18,571 feet with Dawn in April. The trail log is on the blog, including the parts that went badly and the part where I asked the guides too many questions.`,
    href: '/blog/everest-base-camp-summit/',
    external: false,
    cta: 'Read the trail log',
  },
  {
    no: '26-CV-0020',
    name: "AI Dungeon Master's Screen",
    status: 'Stayed, indefinitely',
    tone: 'hold',
    note: `A prototype screen for running 5e: lore lookups and improvisation help for the person behind the cardboard. It has never earned a dollar and it isn't finished, and I'm in no hurry about either.`,
    href: null,
    external: false,
    cta: 'Quiet build',
  },
  {
    no: '26-CV-1000',
    name: 'Puerto Rico AI Community',
    status: 'Active',
    tone: 'go',
    note: `President of the island's AI community (unpaid, obviously), now past 1,000 different people through the door. We meet every other month, it's free, and we argue in both languages until something useful falls out. Come to one!`,
    href: 'https://praicommunity.org/',
    external: true,
    cta: 'Join the next one',
  },
];

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// FINDINGS. The verdict, on the plaintiff, because he bought all of it.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const findings = [
  `The plaintiff bought all of it voluntarily, on purchase orders he signed, in several cases after reading the instructions and in 15 cases after writing them.`,
  `Paragraph 6 is admitted. The plaintiff re-orders the sled at 5AM, through an agent, which the Court finds is the same thing as ordering it himself.`,
  `The products mostly did what the manual said. The Court has reviewed 25 years of evidence and finds that the failures happened in the space between the sales cycle and the manual, and notes that the plaintiff wrote the manual, so he had the least excuse of anyone in the room.`,
  `The plaintiff's actual complaint, which he never filed, is that nobody told the finance team any of this before the deployment. The Court finds that the plaintiff is now the person whose job it is to tell them, from a stage, for a fee, and that he appears to enjoy it.`,
];
---

<BaseLayout>
  <WeeklyAnimation />

  <!-- ================= DOCKET STRIP ================= -->
  <div class="docket-strip" role="presentation">
    <div class="docket-inner">
      <span class="docket-item docket-mark">Roske v. Acme</span>
      <span class="docket-item">Case No. {CASE_NO}</span>
      <span class="docket-item">District Court of the Canyon, Desert Division</span>
      <span class="docket-item docket-filed">Filed 29 Aug 2026, 5:00 AM AST</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ================= HERO: THE CAPTION PAGE ================= -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="hero-kicker">Roske.AI | Case file | Week of 29 August 2026</p>

        <div class="caption" aria-label="Case caption">
          <div class="cap-parties">
            <p class="cap-party">EDWARD ROSKE, an individual,</p>
            <p class="cap-role">Plaintiff,</p>
            <p class="cap-vs">v.</p>
            <p class="cap-party">ACME, and every vendor who ever sold him a single source of truth, DOES 1 through 30,</p>
            <p class="cap-role">Defendants.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-brackets" aria-hidden="true">)<br/>)<br/>)<br/>)<br/>)<br/>)<br/>)<br/>)</div>
          <div class="cap-right">
            <p class="cap-no">Case No. {CASE_NO}</p>
            <p class="cap-title">Complaint for damages</p>
            <p class="cap-note">Jury trial demanded. The plaintiff would like witnesses.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h1 class="case-h1">
          <span class="case-word">Roske</span>
          <span class="case-vs">v.</span>
          <span class="case-word">Acme</span>
        </h1>

        <p class="hero-sub">{theme.hero.subtitle}</p>
        <p class="hero-desc">{theme.hero.description}</p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a href="#exhibits" class="btn-solid">Read the exhibits</a>
          <a href={theme.hero.ctaLink} class="btn-line">{theme.hero.ctaText}</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="hero-fig">
        <div class="hero-frame">
          <span class="stamp stamp-hero" aria-hidden="true">Exhibit 1</span>
          <img
            src={`/images/${theme.hero.heroImage}`}
            alt={theme.hero.imageAlt}
            width="1600"
            height="900"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
            class="hero-img"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption class="hero-cap">
          Exhibit 1. The plaintiff, in transit. The rocket fires out of both ends, which the
          catalog listed as a feature, and the briefcase contains the catalog. He has ordered this
          sled every Saturday since February (about 25 times so far) and this is the first
          photograph in which he appears to be enjoying it.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <!-- standing stub -->
    <div class="standing" aria-label="Plaintiff's standing">
      <p class="standing-label">Plaintiff's standing, as entered</p>
      <div class="standing-grid">
        {standing.map(s => (
          <div class="standing-item">
            <span class="standing-v">{s.v}</span>
            <span class="standing-k">{s.k}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= LATEST CONTENT (permanent) ================= -->
  <LatestContent
    eyebrow="Recent filings"
    heading="Entered into <em>the record.</em>"
    deck="New writing and new video briefs, in the order they were filed. The clerk accepts everything and reads about half."
  />

  <!-- ================= BOOK EDWARD (permanent) ================= -->
  <div class="retain">
    <p class="retain-plate">The plaintiff is also available as a witness</p>
    <SpeakerCTA eyebrow="Expert witness for hire" />
  </div>

  <!-- ================= THE COMPLAINT ================= -->
  <section class="complaint" id="complaint">
    <div class="complaint-head">
      <p class="sec-eyebrow">Filing one</p>
      <h2 class="sec-h2">The complaint.</h2>
      <p class="sec-deck">
        Plaintiff, appearing on his own behalf because no lawyer would take this, alleges as
        follows, and every allegation below is true except the one where it's a lawsuit. (Edward,
        you're describing a 25-year career as a series of purchases. You did the buying. Nobody made
        you build a company on it, and nobody in 2026 is making you build the plumbing for the next
        version either, which you're doing anyway, at night, for fun, and which you have described
        to Dawn as work.)
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="plead">
      {complaint.map((p, i) => (
        <li class="plead-p">
          <span class="plead-n">{i + 1}.</span>
          <p class="plead-text" set:html={p} />
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= EXHIBITS A THROUGH F ================= -->
  <section class="exhibits" id="exhibits">
    <div class="exhibits-head">
      <p class="sec-eyebrow">Filing two</p>
      <h2 class="sec-h2">Exhibits A through F.</h2>
      <p class="sec-deck">
        The career, refiled as evidence. Each exhibit was entered by the plaintiff against his
        own interest, and every one of them links to the rest of the paperwork if you'd like to
        spend your Saturday the way I apparently spent 25 years.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="exhibits-grid">
      <figure class="witness">
        <div class="witness-frame">
          <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Exhibit 2</span>
          <img src="/images/roske-v-acme/witness-stand.jpg" width="1200" height="1600" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
            alt="Edward Roske in a charcoal suit and his blue fedora standing in a wood-paneled courtroom witness box, right hand raised to be sworn in, his left hand resting on a thick, battered mail-order catalog." />
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          Exhibit 2. The plaintiff being sworn in on the catalog, which is the only book in the
          building he has read cover to cover. The hand on the catalog is the same hand that
          signed the purchase orders, and the Court noticed.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <ol class="ex-list">
        {exhibits.map(e => (
          <li class="ex">
            <div class="ex-tab">
              <span class="ex-letter">{e.letter}</span>
              <span class="ex-caption">{CASE_NO} | Ex. {e.letter}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ex-body">
              <h3 class="ex-title">{e.title}</h3>
              <p class="ex-desc" set:html={e.desc} />
              <a href={e.href} class="ex-link">{e.cta}</a>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= DELIVERY (full bleed) ================= -->
  <section class="delivery">
    <figure class="delivery-fig">
      <img src="/images/roske-v-acme/canyon-delivery.jpg" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
        alt="Edward Roske in a dark suit and blue fedora at the edge of a red-rock canyon, holding a clipboard and a crowbar, checking a tall stack of freshly delivered wooden crates marked with arrows and fragile symbols, a small dust cloud settling on the canyon floor far below." />
      <figcaption class="delivery-cap">
        <span class="stamp stamp-cap" aria-hidden="true">Exhibit 3</span>
        <span class="delivery-text">
          Exhibit 3. Delivery. Everything arrives in crates, on the edge, with arrows that say which
          way is up and nothing that says what's inside. That dust cloud on the canyon floor is last
          week's order, and I have the clipboard to prove I signed for this one too.
        </span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= THE CATALOG ================= -->
  <section class="catalog" id="catalog">
    <div class="catalog-head">
      <p class="sec-eyebrow">Filing three</p>
      <h2 class="sec-h2">The catalog.</h2>
      <p class="sec-deck">
        If you run a finance organization you have bought at least 4 of these, and one of them is
        in a data center right now with your name on the purchase order. Every plate below is a
        real promise from a real sales cycle I sat in, with the product names removed because I
        would like to keep being invited to their conferences (they have good coffee, and they
        have stopped seating me near the product managers).
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="catalog-inner">
      <figure class="plate-fig">
        <div class="plate-frame">
          <span class="plate-no">Plate 1</span>
          <img src="/images/roske-v-acme/catalog-plate.jpg" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
            alt="A vintage catalog-style studio photograph of Edward Roske in a dark suit and blue fedora, smiling like a salesman and gesturing at a refrigerator-sized coiled steel spring bolted to a wooden crate with a big red lever on the side." />
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          Plate 1. Item 1000, the Enterprise Spring (not listed below, discontinued after the
          incident). The man in the plate has the smile of somebody who has not yet pulled the red
          lever, and I'd like it noted that I've pulled the red lever 25 years' worth of times
          since this was taken.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="catalog-masthead">
        <p class="cat-brand">Apex Enterprise Supply Co.</p>
        <p class="cat-tag">Purveyors of fine single sources of truth to the Office of the CFO since 1949. Allow 6 to 8 quarters for delivery.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="plates">
        {catalog.map(c => (
          <li class="plate">
            <header class="plate-head">
              <span class="plate-item">No. {c.no}</span>
              {c.isNew && <span class="plate-new">New for 2026</span>}
            </header>
            <div class="plate-schem" aria-hidden="true">
              {c.icon === 'source' && (
                <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="schem"><rect x="30" y="30" width="40" height="40" rx="3"/><path d="M10 50h20M70 50h20M50 10v20M50 70v20"/><path d="M26 46l4 4-4 4M74 46l-4 4 4 4M46 26l4-4 4 4M46 74l4 4 4-4"/></svg>
              )}
              {c.icon === 'self' && (
                <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="schem"><path d="M15 25h70l-25 30v25l-20-8V55z"/><path d="M50 55v10"/><circle cx="50" cy="16" r="5"/></svg>
              )}
              {c.icon === 'close' && (
                <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="schem"><circle cx="50" cy="55" r="32"/><path d="M50 55V33M50 55l16 10"/><path d="M40 12h20M50 12v11"/><path d="M22 28l-6-6M78 28l6-6"/></svg>
              )}
              {c.icon === 'plug' && (
                <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="schem"><rect x="30" y="40" width="40" height="32" rx="4"/><path d="M40 40V22M60 40V22M50 72v16"/><path d="M14 88h72"/></svg>
              )}
              {c.icon === 'gauge' && (
                <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="schem"><path d="M15 70a35 35 0 0 1 70 0"/><path d="M50 70L70 42"/><circle cx="50" cy="70" r="4"/><path d="M22 60l6 2M78 60l-6 2M50 36v6"/><path d="M15 84h70"/></svg>
              )}
              {c.icon === 'chip' && (
                <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="schem"><rect x="28" y="28" width="44" height="44" rx="4"/><rect x="40" y="40" width="20" height="20"/><path d="M38 28V14M50 28V14M62 28V14M38 86V72M50 86V72M62 86V72M28 38H14M28 50H14M28 62H14M86 38H72M86 50H72M86 62H72"/></svg>
              )}
            </div>
            <h3 class="plate-name">{c.name}</h3>
            <p class="plate-sell">{c.sell}</p>
            <p class="plate-got"><span class="plate-got-k">Received:</span> {c.got}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= THE DEPOSITION ================= -->
  <section class="depo" id="deposition">
    <div class="depo-head">
      <p class="sec-eyebrow">Filing four</p>
      <h2 class="sec-h2">Deposition of the plaintiff.</h2>
      <p class="sec-deck">
        The questions people actually ask, taken under oath, in a room with one lamp. Volume I.
        Appearances: for the plaintiff, the plaintiff. For the defendants, also the plaintiff,
        since he wrote their manuals and can still find the chapter.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="depo-fig">
      <img src="/images/roske-v-acme/deposition.jpg" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
